{"file": "C:/Users/Garrett/Sports/docs/arxiv-program/research/2026-09-21/arxiv-deep/0034-darts-analysis.md", "equation": "Two evaluation approaches, each applied at game start and at each round start: (1) **Brier scores** (proper scoring; defined in §2.3 as mean squared error B(π) = (1/n)Σ(π_t − σ_t)²); (2) **head-to-head betting game**: model α sets odds, model β bets, profit decides; \"betting edge\" = positive net payout; possible for both models to have edges — higher total profit wins. Bets placed per round (Tables 5, 7a) and game-start-only (Tables 6, 7b). Baselines: the five models against each other (no external baseline). The paper is 16 pages, 8 figures. Worked example (Table 2): Alice vs. Bob, model-B payouts −0.0275 + 0.0624 = +0.0349 vs. reversed −0.018 → model β superior.", "page_or_eqnum": null, "wave": 9122}
